.TH README 1 "September 2026" "readme 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
readme \- open the nearest README file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B readme
[\fB-hlv\fR] [\fIfilename\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B readme
looks for files named
.B README
or beginning with
.B README.
in the current directory. If none are found, it searches immediate child
directories. Matches are sorted without regard to case.
.PP
Without options, the first match opens with
.BR glow (1)
when available, or with
.BR less (1)
otherwise.
.PP
When supplied,
.I filename
is opened directly when it is a file. When it is a directory,
.B readme
opens the first README in that directory.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I filename
A file to open directly, or a directory whose README to open. Relative paths
are resolved from the current directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h
Show the help screen.
.TP
.B -l
List matching README files instead of opening one.
.TP
.B -v
Show the version number.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Open a README in an immediate child directory:
.nf
.B readme timinal
.fi
.TP
List matching README files:
.nf
.B readme -l
.fi
